    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Principal Components: Intuition\"\ndescription: \"A simple graphical illustration to give some intuition about what a Principal Component Analysis does.\"\ndate: 2017-06-24\nauthor: \"Athos Damiani\"\ncategories: [\"concepts\", \"pca\", \"principal components\", \"plotly\"]\nimage: componentes_principais.webp\n---\n\n\n\nPrincipal components are widely used in statistical modeling, but their rigorous mathematical definition makes PCA look like a more abstract concept than we can grasp, especially when people say **\"maximize the total variance\"** and **\"reduce the dimensionality\"**. The first reaction is a big \"HUH?\".\n\nBelow are some 3D plots that give a good illustration of what these two statements mean and, even though it's a simple example, they'll help extrapolate the idea to more complex problems.\n\n1) The first plot is the representation with **100% of the information** in three dimensions.\n2) The second plot is how the same dataset looks with one dimension less (**dimensionality reduction**).\n3) When we drop a dimension, we lose information (it's no longer **100% of the total variance**), and this loss is measured by the variance explained by the dimensions we left behind.\n4) The first two dimensions project the data so that they show the **maximum total variance** possible in only two dimensions.\n\n\n**packages for the examples**\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(magrittr)\nlibrary(tidyr)\nlibrary(dplyr)\n```\n:::\n\n\nNote: don't forget to rotate the plots! =)\n\n## Example 1 - Tetrahedron\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\na <- 1\ntetraedro <- data.frame( x = c(a * sqrt(3)/3, - a * sqrt(3)/6, - a * sqrt(3)/6, 0),\n                         y = c(0, - a/2, a/2, 0),\n                         z = c(0, 0, 0, a * sqrt(6)/3),\n                         cor = c(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"),\n                         id = 1:4)\n\ntetraedro_linhas <- combn(x = tetraedro$id, m = 2) %>%\n  t %>%\n  as.data.frame.matrix %>%\n  set_names(c(\"id1\", \"id2\")) %>%\n  mutate(id_par = 1:n()) %>%\n  gather(id_ordem, id, id1, id2) %>%\n  left_join(tetraedro, by = \"id\") %>%\n  arrange(id_ordem)\n```\n:::\n\n\n**Contribution of the components to the total variance**\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ntetraedro_pc <- prcomp(tetraedro %>% dplyr::select(x, y, z)) # PCA happens here\nknitr::kable(summary(tetraedro_pc)$importance)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|                       |       PC1|       PC2|       PC3|\n|:----------------------|---------:|---------:|---------:|\n|Standard deviation     | 0.4082483| 0.4082483| 0.4082483|\n|Proportion of Variance | 0.3333300| 0.3333300| 0.3333300|\n|Cumulative Proportion  | 0.3333300| 0.6666700| 1.0000000|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**3 dimensions (100% of the variance)**\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(plotly)\n\nplot_ly(tetraedro_linhas, x = ~x, y = ~y, z = ~z) %>%\n  add_lines() %>%\n  add_markers()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-f723208b5186d5c083a4\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-f723208b5186d5c083a4\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"1d554a51a46\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"1d554a51a46\",\"attrs\":{\"1d554a51a46\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"z\":{},\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"inherit\":true},\"1d554a51a46.1\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"z\":{},\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"markers\",\"inherit\":true}},\"layout\":{\"margin\":{\"b\":40,\"l\":60,\"t\":25,\"r\":10},\"scene\":{\"xaxis\":{\"title\":\"x\"},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":\"y\"},\"zaxis\":{\"title\":\"z\"}},\"hovermode\":\"closest\",\"showlegend\":true},\"source\":\"A\",\"config\":{\"modeBarButtonsToAdd\":[\"hoverclosest\",\"hovercompare\"],\"showSendToCloud\":false},\"data\":[{\"x\":[-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,0,0,0,0.57735026918962573,0.57735026918962573,0.57735026918962573],\"y\":[-0.5,-0.5,0.5,-0.5,0.5,0.5,0,0,0,0,0,0],\"z\":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0.81649658092772592,0.81649658092772592,0.81649658092772592,0,0,0],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"}},\"error_y\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"error_x\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"frame\":null},{\"x\":[0.57735026918962573,0.57735026918962573,0.57735026918962573,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,-0.28867513459481287,0,-0.28867513459481287,0,0],\"y\":[0,0,0,-0.5,-0.5,0.5,-0.5,0.5,0,0.5,0,0],\"z\":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0.81649658092772592,0,0.81649658092772592,0.81649658092772592],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"markers\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"}},\"error_y\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"error_x\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"frame\":null}],\"highlight\":{\"on\":\"plotly_click\",\"persistent\":false,\"dynamic\":false,\"selectize\":false,\"opacityDim\":0.20000000000000001,\"selected\":{\"opacity\":1},\"debounce\":0},\"shinyEvents\":[\"plotly_hover\",\"plotly_click\",\"plotly_selected\",\"plotly_relayout\",\"plotly_brushed\",\"plotly_brushing\",\"plotly_clickannotation\",\"plotly_doubleclick\",\"plotly_deselect\",\"plotly_afterplot\",\"plotly_sunburstclick\"],\"base_url\":\"https://plot.ly\"},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**2 dimensions (67% of the variance)**\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ntetraedro_pc_pred <- tetraedro_pc %>% predict %>% as.data.frame\nplot_ly(tetraedro_pc_pred, x = ~PC2, y = ~PC3, z = ~PC3) %>%\n  add_lines() %>%\n  add_markers()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-54a7f0f2a9cff9827191\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-54a7f0f2a9cff9827191\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"1d55414c353b2\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"1d55414c353b2\",\"attrs\":{\"1d55414c353b2\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"z\":{},\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"inherit\":true},\"1d55414c353b2.1\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"z\":{},\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"markers\",\"inherit\":true}},\"layout\":{\"margin\":{\"b\":40,\"l\":60,\"t\":25,\"r\":10},\"scene\":{\"xaxis\":{\"title\":\"PC2\"},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":\"PC3\"},\"zaxis\":{\"title\":\"PC3\"}},\"hovermode\":\"closest\",\"showlegend\":true},\"source\":\"A\",\"config\":{\"modeBarButtonsToAdd\":[\"hoverclosest\",\"hovercompare\"],\"showSendToCloud\":false},\"data\":[{\"x\":[-0.20412414523193148,-0.20412414523193148,-0.20412414523193148,0.61237243569579447],\"y\":[-0.57735026918962573,0.28867513459481287,0.28867513459481287,0],\"z\":[-0.57735026918962573,0.28867513459481287,0.28867513459481287,0],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"}},\"error_y\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"error_x\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(31,119,180,1)\"},\"frame\":null},{\"x\":[-0.20412414523193148,-0.20412414523193148,-0.20412414523193148,0.61237243569579447],\"y\":[-0.57735026918962573,0.28867513459481287,0.28867513459481287,0],\"z\":[-0.57735026918962573,0.28867513459481287,0.28867513459481287,0],\"type\":\"scatter3d\",\"mode\":\"markers\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"}},\"error_y\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"error_x\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"line\":{\"color\":\"rgba(255,127,14,1)\"},\"frame\":null}],\"highlight\":{\"on\":\"plotly_click\",\"persistent\":false,\"dynamic\":false,\"selectize\":false,\"opacityDim\":0.20000000000000001,\"selected\":{\"opacity\":1},\"debounce\":0},\"shinyEvents\":[\"plotly_hover\",\"plotly_click\",\"plotly_selected\",\"plotly_relayout\",\"plotly_brushed\",\"plotly_brushing\",\"plotly_clickannotation\",\"plotly_doubleclick\",\"plotly_deselect\",\"plotly_afterplot\",\"plotly_sunburstclick\"],\"base_url\":\"https://plot.ly\"},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n## Example 2 - A cool shape\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nx <- c()\ny <- c()\nz <- c()\nc <- c()\n\nfor (i in 1:62) {\n  r <- 20 * cos(i / 20)\n  x <- c(x, r * cos(i))\n  y <- c(y, r * sin(i))\n  z <- c(z, i)\n  c <- c(c, i)\n}\n\nforma_legal <- data.frame(x, y, z, c)\n```\n:::\n\n\n**Contribution of the components to the total variance**\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nforma_legal_pc <- prcomp(forma_legal %>% dplyr::select(x, y, z)) # PCA happens here\nknitr::kable(summary(forma_legal_pc)$importance)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|                       |      PC1|      PC2|      PC3|\n|:----------------------|--------:|--------:|--------:|\n|Standard deviation     | 18.04936| 10.13750| 9.854732|\n|Proportion of Variance |  0.61975|  0.19550| 0.184750|\n|Cumulative Proportion  |  0.61975|  0.81525| 1.000000|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**3 dimensions (100% of the variance)**\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nplot_ly(forma_legal, x = ~x, y = ~y, z = ~z, type = \"scatter3d\", mode = \"markers+lines\",\n        line = list(width = 6, color = ~c, colorscale = 'Viridis'),\n        marker = list(size = 3.5, color = ~c, colorscale = 'Greens',\n                      cmin = -20, cmax = 50))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-cfee95381032b5f7f88d\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></